From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The mirrored copies go with their map, begun while the game
 reads it (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Riding north on the Cycling Road the game still stuttered (a log of
2026-11-06): game frames of 47 to 63 ms as each new row of maps came in,
the 3DS's screen held a moment and the player seen to jump. On the PC
(riding north from 299,676, Route 206's trainers taken away):

- A map's mirrored copy (patch 0069) was kept in the slot of the quadrant
  its map had. When the game moved its maps to the other quadrants (the
  player across a map's middle) the copy didn't match its slot and was made
  again, all at once, the map being in the view: 4.4 to 4.8 ms.
- The new row's map came into the view as soon as the game had it (it's
  read whole for the wider view while the game reads it, patch 0098), and
  its copy was made all at once then: 3.6 to 6.5 ms.

Now:

- The copies are kept in 8 places, found by their map (where, its matrix,
  its land data), side and rows, whatever quadrant the map is in: a copy
  goes with its map, and a map's both sides are kept (the player crossing
  its middle, on the Cycling Road from one lane to the other).
- While the game still reads a map that's read whole for the wider view,
  its copy is begun from that whole copy (the same land data, bound to the
  field's own textures), a little a scene, and carried on from the game's
  own model once it has it.
- A copy with no rows moved over that isn't made when it's seen goes on
  being made a little a scene, and meanwhile the whole map is drawn
  mirrored (Port_RenderMirroredWhole, with the river's waves turned round
  as the copy's are): the same picture, more for the 3D to throw away for
  a few scenes. One with rows moved over is still finished at once.
- A copy's model gets the area lighting's global colours (outdoors), as the
  game's own maps do once it has them: a copy made the scene its map came
  in had been made before the game set them, its mirrored side a shade off
  from the rest till the next time it was made.

On the PC riding north: no copy is made again as the maps move; 579's
begun from its whole copy and finished in 1.6 ms the scene it's first
seen (rows moved over; 3.6 ms before), 549's made before it's seen (6.5
ms before). The ride's pictures are the same but for the mirrored strip by
the left edge from 299,646 north, now the same as a warp there shows (the
lighting). Riding across the middle at 299-306,598 (both sides' copies
made while seen, the whole map drawn mirrored meanwhile), riding south from
300,590, and Valley Windworks at 250,648, 246,652, 250,660 and 236,650:
the same pictures.

